// @emit-error print takes exactly one argument
// CONTRACT: `print` is an OVERLOAD SET over the printable runtime reps, not a variadic
// or polymorphic function — its arity is exactly ONE. The checker arm walks and checks
// every argument (so a type error inside any of them still surfaces) but does not count
// them, so the arity verdict is the EMITTER's: a loud `@emit-error`, not silent codegen.
// Pins the arity half of the rendered builtin signature
// `(i32 | i64 | f32 | f64 | boolean | string) -> void` that the LSP and playground show.
print(1, 2)
